# Cheap agent routing (owner is not a developer)

The product owner describes bugs in plain English and does **not** know file names.
Your job is to map the symptom to a small file list and **stay there**. Do not explore the whole repo.

## Token budget (mandatory)

- Prefer `rg` / `Grep` for exact symbols over reading huge files.
- Do **not** read all of `src/main.js` unless a targeted search failed. Prefer `Grep` + `Read` with offset/limit around the hit.
- Skip `website/` unless the bug is about asperahub.com / the marketing site.
- Skip AI (`src/ai/`), forward, Zoho CRM, extensions, and PDF code unless the report mentions them.
- One bug per change set. Do not “also clean up” unrelated areas.
- If the user says **fix only**, **I'll test first**, or **don't release yet** — patch + commit/push/PR only; **do not** `npm run make` or publish a GitHub release until they confirm.
- If the user only asks for advice (no code change), answer in text — do not open a feature branch or ship.

## Symptom → where to look first

| User says (examples) | Open these first |
|---|---|
| Link in WhatsApp / Arattai opens wrong, nowhere, or replaces chat; Hub tab; Drive / Google link | `src/guestNav.js`, `src/guestNavigation.js`, then `handleOutboundOrNewWindowLink` / `openUrlAsHubAppTab` in `src/main.js` |
| Update check failed / Feed 404 / latest.json | `src/updater.js`, `scripts/publish-update.mjs`, GitHub release assets — usually upload missing `latest.json`, not a big code rewrite |
| Website / asperahub.com / download page | `website/index.html` only (+ `website/assets/` if images) |
| Pin / Hub pin / open chat from pin | `src/whatsappPinOpen.js`, `src/guestInbox.js`, pin helpers in `src/main.js` |
| Safe Mode / WhatsApp automation blocked | `src/whatsappSafeMode.js` |
| Find / Ctrl+F / search highlight | Find-bar related files (`src/findBar*`, search in `src/main.js` / renderer) |
| Google Web search / Ctrl+E | `src/webSearch.js`, `src/webSearch*` |
| Aspera AI / Summarize / Suggest reply / languages | `src/ai/` only |
| Forward WhatsApp ↔ Arattai | `src/forwardHub.js` |
| Notification / tray / badge / mute | notification / tray code in `src/main.js` + notif center HTML |
| Settings UI / theme / lock | settings sections in renderer + store |
| Crash on start / blank window | `src/main.js` window create + guest lifecycle (`src/guestLifecycle.js`) |

## How to reply to the owner

- Use plain language. No “refactor the abstraction” jargon.
- Say what you fixed in one short sentence and how to install/test (version or `.deb` link when shipped).
- If you need a clarifying detail, ask **one** yes/no or A/B question — not a questionnaire.

## Prompt the owner can paste (you may remind them)

When starting a bug, they can write:

> Bug: \<what app: WhatsApp / Arattai / Gmail / Zoho / website\>  
> What I did: \<one sentence\>  
> What should happen: \<one sentence\>  
> What happens instead: \<one sentence\>  
> Version: \<e.g. 0.5.17\>  
> Fix only first — wait for me to test before release.
